/, built from `docs/site/` by `.github/workflows/docs.yml`):\n\n1. **Overview (`docs/site/index.md`): add a diagram of the process**, triage → workers → reviewers → merge, with scanners feeding triage and the review-fix loop back to the worker.\n2. **Split `docs/site/roles.md`** into a roles overview plus one page per role kind: **scanners, triage, workers, reviewers**.\n\n## Design\n**Diagram**\n- Use a Mermaid flowchart. Enable it in `mkdocs.yml` with `pymdownx.superfences` and a `mermaid` custom fence (`format: !!python/name:pymdownx.superfences.fence_code_format`), as MkDocs Material documents. `pymdown-extensions` is already in `docs/site/requirements.txt`; add no new dependency.\n- Content: issue → (scanners file issues) → triage (lead, engineer, optional roles) → `plan.md` → human `ard:approved` (when `require_approval`) → worker (branch, tests, draft PR) → reviewers → changes: back to the worker (review rounds, capped by `max_review_rounds`) / all approve: PR ready → merger (reviews at head, checks green, protected paths need a human) → merged, issue closed. Show `ard:needs-human` as the exit from any stage.\n- Keep it to what `docs/proposal.md` says; the proposal's architecture flowchart is the source of truth.\n- Place it under \"The loop\", before the numbered list; keep the list.\n\n**Roles pages**\n- `docs/site/roles/index.md` (nav \"Roles overview\"): what a role is, the four kinds, where role directories live (`.ard/<kind>/<name>/`), the role file, the write allowlist, writing a prompt: the shared material now in `roles.md` (\"Writing a role prompt\", \"The role file\", \"The write allowlist\").\n- `docs/site/roles/scanners.md`, `triage.md`, `workers.md`, `reviewers.md`: for each kind, what it does, its inputs and outputs, its labels, the starter roles of that kind (from \"Starter roles\"), and its main config overrides. Draw on `docs/proposal.md` (the scanner, triage, worker and reviewer loop sections, and the starter role paragraphs). User-facing: what a maintainer needs, not implementation detail.\n- `mkdocs.yml` nav: replace `Roles: roles.md` with a `Roles` section listing the overview and the four pages. Remove `roles.md`; update every link to it across `docs/site/` (and the README if it links there) so `mkdocs build --strict` passes.\n\n**Out of scope:** a page per individual role (lead, engineer, eng-review, ...); docs outside `docs/site/` beyond fixing links.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- The overview page renders a Mermaid diagram of scanners → triage → approval → workers → reviewers (with the fix loop) → merger, plus the `ard:needs-human` exit.\n- The site nav has a Roles section: Roles overview, Scanners, Triage, Workers, Reviewers. `roles.md` is gone and nothing links to it.\n- No content from the old `roles.md` is lost.\n- `make docs-check` passes (`mkdocs build --strict` and the Go drift test).\n\nNote: #349 (PR #401) is changing `getting-started.md`, the README and the onboarding runbook now; avoid those files except for link fixes, and expect a small rebase.\n\n# Plan for #402\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Steps\n1. `mkdocs.yml` (edit): add after `plugins:` a `markdown_extensions:` block with `admonition`-free minimal config: `pymdownx.superfences` with `custom_fences: [{name: mermaid, class: mermaid, format: !!python/name:pymdownx.superfences.fence_code_format}]`. No new dependency (`pymdown-extensions` is in `docs/site/requirements.txt`). The build stays green because nothing uses the fence yet.\n2. `docs/site/roles/index.md` (new, nav \"Roles overview\"): move from `docs/site/roles.md` the intro, the directory/type table, the agent/executable/Docker paragraph, and the sections \"Writing a role prompt\", \"The role file\", \"The write allowlist\" verbatim. Replace \"Starter roles\" with a short list linking to the four kind pages (`scanners.md`, `triage.md`, `workers.md`, `reviewers.md`, relative to `roles/`). Keep the sentence that role directories are protected paths in the recommended config.\n